@startuml
' Squatm3gator System Architecture

package "squatm3gator System" {
  [Web UI] as web_ui
  [HTTP API] as http_api
  [WebSocket Channel] as websocket
  [Background Consumer] as consumer
  [squatm3 Engine] as squatm3
  [Redis] as redis
  [GoDaddy API] as godaddy
  
  ' Internal component relationships
  web_ui --> http_api : requests
  http_api --> redis : publish jobs
  http_api --> websocket : session updates
  consumer --> redis : consume jobs\npublish results
  consumer --> squatm3 : execute domain\ngeneration
  consumer --> websocket : stream results
  http_api --> consumer : start background\nprocessing
  websocket --> web_ui : async updates
  
  ' External service integration
  consumer ..> godaddy : optional domain\navailability check
}

note right of redis
  Redis serves as the message broker
  for job queue and result reporting
end note

note right of consumer
  Background consumer thread started
  by API process listens for jobs
  and executes squatm3 engine
end note

note right of squatm3
  Wrapped third-party CLI engine
  for domain generation execution
end note

note top of godaddy
  Optional integration for 
  domain availability checking
  using configured credentials
end note

@enduml